  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowered Miskito Women Conserving the Central American Scarlet Macaw</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) training 20 Miskito women from six local villages in forest patrols, handi-crafts and as environmental educators for parrot conservation; (2) supporting an indigenous womens ranger team to monitor and protect wild nest sites of macaws closer to the villages while the men continue patrols in more remote locations; (3) led by female rangers, develop wildlife and parrot clubs with local school children as well as a community parrot festival; and (4) selection of four women with leadership potential to participate as Ambassadors for the community and parrot conservation in a national and international biodiversity conference.</narrative>
  </description>
